---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About — Blue Collar Labs" description="Founded on a job site, not in a boardroom. The mission, the founder, the operating principles behind Blue Collar Labs.">
  <section class="container-wide pt-20 pb-12">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold">Founded on a job site.<br><span class="text-volt-500">Not in a boardroom.</span></h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-steel-300">Blue Collar Labs is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit started by an electrician who got tired of watching $242 billion pour into AI while the trades got nothing. We build, teach, and defend — in that order, in public, with the people whose livelihoods depend on it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container-wide py-8">
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Mission</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold">Close the AI gap for the trades</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-steel-300">Build tools <em>for</em> tradesmen. Teach them <em>with</em> AI. Defend them <em>from</em> AI. Every program is co-designed with working tradespeople and pressure-tested in real shops.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why now</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold">The workforce is aging out</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-steel-300">In NJ alone, three tradespeople retire for every one entering the field. Without better tools and training, shops close, costs rise, and communities lose the people who keep the lights on. AI isn't the enemy — neglect is.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Operating principles</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-steel-300">
          <li>• <strong class="text-white">Built by the user.</strong> No product goes out without a tradesperson writing, using, and breaking it first.</li>
          <li>• <strong class="text-white">Earned + granted.</strong> Revenue from one shop subsidizes access for the next.</li>
          <li>• <strong class="text-white">Measured outcomes.</strong> Time saved, jobs won, shops protected — reported quarterly.</li>
          <li>• <strong class="text-white">Plain language.</strong> If a journeyman can't understand it, we rewrite it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Year 1 targets</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-steel-300">
          <li>• 50 contractors using BUILD tools</li>
          <li>• 100 tradespeople certified in applied AI</li>
          <li>• 10 shops hardened via DEFEND audits</li>
          <li>• First earned-revenue milestone + grant reporting cycle complete</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-wide py-12">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-steel-700/60 bg-steel-800/40 p-8 md:p-10">
      <p class="eyebrow">Founder</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold">Paul Mantello — electrician, founder</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-steel-300">Paul started Blue Collar Labs after years of running jobs with tools that didn't fit the work. The first product, Truck Inventory, was built because he was tired of counting fittings from memory. The nonprofit followed because the problem was bigger than one shop, one truck, one trade.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
